# Manual package implementation - structural slice and exact crypto gate

Task PACC-PHASE6-MANUAL-PACKAGE-GENERATOR-IMPLEMENTATION-1. main / c50b8fb9a7e3293b5e6355fc08459bf85b56857a. Accepted M0-M8 manifest23/23 hashes matched; baseline4730 files. Official executor approved the exact4-file source/CMake/test patch and subsequent public-fixture-only correction. All preimages/postimages are retained. No prior source WIP was restored or overwritten.

## Implemented portable component

src/provisioning/manual_package.c/.h is a bounded private synchronous DATA codec, not a crypto provider or operational generator. All outputs use caller storage; no heap, I/O, native handle, key generation, persistent object, thread, owner or registry is introduced. MP_DATA_ONLY=1 is deliberately distinct from operational success and never means authenticated package, X509 validity, RESOLVED or CURRENT.

- mp_payload_prepare accepts five owned input slices and validates exact config/issuance metadata shapes. It emits canonical ZIP32 STORE: five exact ordered names, fixed headers/timestamps/attributes, checked sizes/offsets, ZIP CRC32, central directory and EOCD. It rereads its own output structurally before publishing used length. It does not validate DER/certificate/key correspondence or authorize private-key use.
- mp_payload_inspect rejects wrong/unexpected/duplicate/traversal names, flags/method/ZIP64/descriptor/extra/comment/attribute variations, lengths/CRC/offset/order mismatch, holes, overlaps, trailing bytes and invalid TLV/name/time shape. On success it returns borrowed slices into the immutable caller input; caller keeps its existing ownership/lease until every consumer finishes. No root pin or secret lease is created by this parser. Direct clear-payload use is for caller-owned offline preparation, or future already-authenticated/quarantined plaintext; no unauthenticated envelope-to-ZIP path exists.
- mp_envelope_prepare frames ALREADY SUPPLIED header/SPKI/ciphertext/tag/signature bytes. It checks exact M2 magic/version/suite/flags/iterations/length relationships before copying. It does NOT encrypt, derive a key, calculate SPKI SHA256, create randomness, parse the RSA SPKI, sign or approve inputs. Even zero/dummy crypto bytes can be inspected as framing DATA; they can never pass authenticated package validation.
- mp_envelope_inspect returns only bounded framing slices, not verified SPKI, signature or plaintext. It rejects unknown version/suite/flags, unapproved iteration count, excess/truncation/trailing lengths. It never decrypts or parses ciphertext as ZIP.
- mp_package_validate calls framing inspection then returns MP_CRYPTO_UNAVAILABLE for every structurally accepted envelope. It accepts/retains no password and never calls private-key/signing APIs. Malformed input/Stop stays rejected. There is no test/backend selector, fake cryptographic success, fallback algorithm or alternate authority.

CMake adds an isolated static library and C90 test target only. The library is NOT linked into papacc_server in any of the four checked build graphs; no CLI dispatcher or product configuration changed. Existing root/C8/issuer/CURRENT/pins/Stop/Session/grants/ED11 guards and formats are byte-identical. Production0.6.4, PST and Browser are unchanged.

## Honest validation scope

Selected Windows3MiB and Legacy2MiB Debug/Release builds pass with zero compiler warnings;17/17 selected suites pass each. New suite2077 assertions covers a synthetic canonical clear archive/framing round trip, standard ZIP CRC32 check value, every single-byte archive mutation, every truncation, explicit traversal/duplicate/unexpected member, unknown version/iterations, invalid DNS/count, capacity and output alias denial, Stop before operation and caller-owned old-buffer coexistence. Synthetic materials/SPKI/tag/signature are PUBLIC INVALID DUMMIES, not real keys/certificates or an authenticated package. No file/package/key/certificate/private signature was generated.

Wrong password, AEAD/tag authenticity, RSA signature, CA/leaf/SAN/issuer/key correspondence and authenticated postvalidation are NOT qualified or reported PASS. For mutated dummy ciphertext/signature the test proves only CRYPTO_UNAVAILABLE, not cryptographic detection. Existing issuer/X509 model suites remain separate evidence, not a package material validator. Initial fixture used forbidden control bytes for correlation and was correctly rejected; only the fixture was corrected to public TEST. Initial diagnostic combined-TU shadow warnings were confined to the temporary diagnostic harness; final project builds are warning-free.

## Ownership / Stop / retention

All calls are synchronous, serialized by the caller and have immutable input/disjoint-output preconditions. Span/alias checks precede writes; used/output availability is cleared on safe entry. Stop denies before work/output. ZIP CRC loops are bounded by accepted member caps; no KDF or asynchronous worker exists here. No claim of NT4 latency, cancellation during KDF, or full live Stop qualification is made.

No free, wipe, pin release, generation retirement or result reconciliation is performed by this library. That prevents a data codec from claiming destruction or releasing another owner's memory. Caller-owned output may contain plaintext under future secret use; used0 is not wiping/destruction. Any failed/partial output stays unpublishable, and its existing owner must retain/wipe it using reviewed facilities only after factual quiescence. Runtime secret integration remains denied until that lifecycle/credit is actually connected. No secret was used in current tests.

## Remaining backend/authority binding - no normative reapproval of suite needed

Accepted M1 requires selected/licensed/pinned vetted crypto implementations and known-answer/cross-provider/target proof before secret integration. The existing issuer CNG adapter signs CA-purpose X509 under denied authority; it cannot be reused as a package-purpose signer or client private-key exporter. No qualified Accelerator adapter for the complete PBKDF2/ChaCha20-Poly1305/dedicated-package-signature pipeline was found. Browser BearSSL source is supporting candidate evidence, not an Accelerator dependency/artifact or permission to invent a PBKDF2 implementation. No algorithm is replaced or handwritten to manufacture a green test.

Next functional slice must bind real vetted hash/KDF/AEAD/public signature validation with bounded cancellation and non-elidable cleanup, preserving exact accepted parameters and independent signer trust. Private package signing and server-side client-key generation need actual dedicated purpose/admin/root authority and separate real-effect authorization; current task forbids those effects. Select and qualify concrete artifacts under exact executor review rather than reopen M0-M8 by default.

Before any operational preparation, hold actual same-root CURRENT/source/issuer pins, approved name/server/recipient/policy/signer tuple, reserved serial and material/provider ownership. Build metadata from those actual sources; raw TLV values are never authority. CURRENT_FACTUAL remains PENDING_EXTERNAL_ENVIRONMENT. Never accept a caller boolean or a synthetic fixture as substitute. Protected staging/delivery/revoke/status integration must use the same root/worker/CLI and versioned approved records; no private plaintext file or shadow registry. CLI remains unchanged until those facts are connected.

## Browser handoff, no Browser changes

The same accepted M0-M8 suite applies to simple import while advanced separate-file import stays intact. The new header is a reference data boundary, not a new public wire/API or proof that VC6/NT4 compiles it. Current implementation uses modern stdint/uintptr and C90 syntax; actual VC6 compatibility shim/build and target crypto remain NOT_QUALIFIED.

Required Browser sequence after authorized adaptation: bounded immutable file acquisition -> framing inspection -> independently approved signer purpose/full-SPKI trust and real RSA signature verification -> exact PBKDF2 and AEAD with quarantined output -> only after tag success, strict ZIP/TLV/material validation -> exact certificate/key/CA/issuer/time/server/policy confirmation -> existing material/store_prepare/gate/generation/ActiveConfiguration/candidate_committed/Reference/leases pipeline. No plaintext disk extraction or second store. mp_payload_inspect slices borrow their archive; copy only where the existing generation owns backing, keep the original owner until all borrows quiesce, then reviewed wipe. Existing validator's local key proof is not complete package/chain/time/purpose validation. Stop/Cancel/UNKNOWN preserve old committed config, retained buffers and original credits. Package import/delivery does not grant admission or prove global single-use/device possession.
